page='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>People comparatives — completed 3D and Kawaii</title><style>CSS</style><main><h1>3D and Kawaii: 96 full-figure comparatives</h1><p class="summary"><strong>48 SVGs per style, covering 24 concepts with male and female variants.</strong> Every changed image was checked against its source. All arrows and annotation shapes are retained; meaningful running, walking, strength and age differences are expressed by posed full figures.</p><p>Finished files are in <code>Library/3D animated cartoon/Comparatives/People</code> and <code>Library/Kawaii/Comparatives/People</code>. This keeps them separate from existing object alternatives. People originals and every existing Library file are unchanged.</p><div class="controls"><select id="style" aria-label="Style"><option>3D animated cartoon</option><option>Kawaii</option></select><select id="concept" aria-label="Concept"></select><select id="gender" aria-label="Gender"><option value="M">Male</option><option value="F">Female</option></select><button id="prev">Previous</button><button id="next">Next</button></div><h2 id="title"></h2><div class="pair"><figure><figcaption>Before — saved comparative</figcaption><img id="before" alt="Original comparative"></figure><figure><figcaption>Finished — full figures</figcaption><img id="after" alt="Finished full-figure comparative"></figure></div><p id="notes"></p><p class="small" id="filelinks"></p><p class="small">Review corrected the initial weaker posture to give visibly drooping arms, and aligned walking sticks to hands and ground. Dirt, odour and crossed-out droplets were repositioned where the full figures required it. Original group counts, arrows, star, turtle, speed marks, fading, height contrasts and other props are retained. Superlative stars and the original two-figure compositions are retained; this pass did not redesign their grammar.</p><h2>What about the other People styles?</h2><p><strong>The approach is applicable to the other People styles too.</strong> A missing root folder does not mean that a style has no full-character artwork. I checked the proposed bases and cleaner, faster and older examples in all 12 outstanding styles. They already contain useful complete characters and poses in their numbered folders.</p><p>My recommendation is to reuse each style’s own characters and posed artwork for the missing Pronouns, Contractions and Comparatives, with Fluent’s meaning-bearing arrows and objects. Keep good existing numbered drawings. Preserve tails, antennae, horns, robot joints, dresses, hats and textures. Clay, Doll and Teddy bear can retain their raster texture; this does not require whole-style SVG tracing. A single standing cutout cannot replace every action pose.</p><p>Flat outlined, Mulberry and Simple anime retain their existing adaptations under your earlier choice. That choice is not evidence that complete figures would be worse in those styles; their existing work is reusable, so a broader change would be a design decision rather than a missing-work fix.</p><details><summary>Read-only examples from all 12 outstanding styles</summary>OTHER</details><h2>All 19 People styles — Task 9 status</h2><p class="notice"><strong>Task 9 is not complete.</strong> This pass completed only the 96 approved 3D/Kawaii comparative changes. It generated no new Pronouns or Contractions. The 12 missing style-root collections below remain explicitly outstanding. Sommi and Sommi clothed are completed and excluded.</p><div class="overflow"><table><thead><tr><th>Style</th><th>Pronouns</th><th>Contractions</th><th>Comparatives</th><th>Remaining work</th></tr></thead><tbody>TABLE</tbody></table></div><p class="small"><a href="visual_review_log.json">Per-image review record</a> · <a href="people_style_status.json">Saved status for every style</a> · <a href="published.json">Publication receipt</a> · <a href="housekeeping.json">Temporary-file cleanup</a></p></main><script>const rows=DATA;const st=document.getElementById('style'),con=document.getElementById('concept'),gen=document.getElementById('gender');const concepts=[...new Set(rows.map(r=>r.concept))];concepts.forEach(c=>con.add(new Option(c,c)));function show(){const r=rows.find(r=>r.style===st.value&&r.concept===con.value&&r.gender===gen.value);document.getElementById('title').textContent=r.style+' — '+r.concept+' ('+(r.gender==='M'?'male':'female')+')';document.getElementById('before').src=r.before_uri;document.getElementById('after').src=r.after_uri;document.getElementById('notes').textContent='Figures: '+r.changes.map(x=>x.pose).join(' / ')+'. All '+r.annotation_primitives+' original annotation shapes retained.';const links=document.getElementById('filelinks');links.replaceChildren();for(const [label,url] of [['Open original SVG',r.before_uri],['Open finished SVG',r.after_uri]]){const a=document.createElement('a');a.textContent=label;a.href=url;links.append(a,document.createTextNode('  '));}}[st,con,gen].forEach(e=>e.onchange=show);document.getElementById('prev').onclick=()=>{con.selectedIndex=(con.selectedIndex+concepts.length-1)%concepts.length;show()};document.getElementById('next').onclick=()=>{con.selectedIndex=(con.selectedIndex+1)%concepts.length;show()};con.value='faster';show();</script></html>'''
